#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inactivate

#% text
# `inactivate(e)` gives `e` with every symbol used as a head (except `list`) replaced by the inert head `inactive(f)`, so that nothing in it is computed; `inactivate(e, p)` replaces only the heads matching the pattern `p` (a symbol, `g | h`, a condition), and the rest of `e` is evaluated. Heads that are calls (`f(x)(y)`) are treated the same way unless `heads: false`. `activate` undoes it.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
inactivate(2 + 2 + 3^2)
#% output
#= inactive(add)(2, 2, inactive(pow)(3, 2))

#% cell
activate(inactivate(2 + 2 + 3^2))
#% output
#= 13

#% cell
inactivate(f(g(h(x)), y, g(z)), g)
#% output
#= f(inactive(g)(h(x)), y, inactive(g)(z))

#% cell
inactivate(sin(pi/3) + cos(pi/3), sin)
#% output
#= 1/2 + inactive(sin)((1/3)*pi)

#% cell
inactivate(f(x)(y) + g(z), heads: false)
#% output
#= inactive(add)(f(x)(y), inactive(g)(z))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `activate`, `inactive`, `quote`
